{#
sharing/shared_calendar.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Somebody's calendar, as much of it as their link reveals — drawn as a calendar,
in the same four views the owner has.

**This template cannot leak, and the reason is what it is given.** `range.days`
holds SharedOccurrence objects, not events: on a busy/free link their `title`,
`location` and `description` are already null and `participants` is already
empty, decided once in ShareLinkReader against the link's checkboxes AND the
event's own privacy. So there is no `if` here that could be forgotten, no tooltip
that could carry a subject, and no data attribute that could carry one into
JavaScript. Adding a field to this page means adding it to the DTO first, which
is where the decision about revealing it has to be made.

Every view below is a rearrangement of exactly those objects and nothing else —
see SharedCalendarRangeBuilder, which has no repository and could not fetch more
if it wanted to.

The counterpart rule: nothing below may reach for `app.user`, a session, or a
CSRF token. See sharing/_layout.html.twig for why. That is also why the chosen
view is in the URL rather than in client state, and why the clock formats arrive
as variables instead of through the `clock` global, which resolves the
signed-in user's preference and therefore asks who is asking.

── Four views, drawn by the owner's own calendar ────────────────────────────

This page was a month grid with a day-by-day list appended under it, which was
itself a correction of a page that had been a list and nothing else. The list
was right that a calendar needs detail somewhere and wrong about where: appended
below a grid it is a second reading of the same fortnight that nobody asked for
twice, and it left the page as the one calendar in the application with no way to
look at a week or a day.

So the list has become the AGENDA — one of four views, reached from a switcher,
exactly as in the calendar it is a window onto. Nothing was thrown away: the
property the old list was built around is kept inside that view, where every
shared day in range is printed including the empty ones, so "free on the 4th" is
a thing the page says rather than a gap the reader has to notice.

**All four are the application's own partials**, not lookalikes:
calendar/_toolbar_shell, _month_shell, _time_grid_shell and _agenda_shell, each
of which the authenticated calendar renders through as well. That is deliberate
to the point of being the constraint the rest of this file is arranged around —
two calendars drawn by two sets of templates drift on the first change to either,
and a public page that looks like a calendar from a different product is exactly
the complaint the shells exist to answer. What this page fills in are the parts
that are about a calendar nobody is signed in to: a chip with no editor behind
it, an agenda row of redacted detail, and the words for a day that is not
published at all.

A busy/free link gets all four views too. The DTOs make that safe without a
single branch here: an entry with nothing revealed renders as the localised
"Busy" wherever a title would go, which is what _entry_chip and _entry_row
already do.

── Days outside the window are not free days ───────────────────────────────

A month has 42 cells; a week has seven columns; a rolling link publishes
fourteen days. The days the link does not cover are drawn dimmed in the grids,
absent from the agenda, and named in a legend on every view, because a blank cell
or an empty column that looked free would make this page claim something about
its owner's diary that its owner never published. In the time-grids they are
drawn without hour lines and say so in words, because twenty-four ruled empty
rows are precisely what a reader reads an availability off.

Paging is bounded to the pages the window actually publishes, in both directions
and on all four views; a step that would leave it is a disabled span rather than
a missing button, so the row does not change shape as you page.

── "Today", conditionally ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

The authenticated toolbar always offers a "today" button. This page dropped it
when it was month-only, on the argument that a control which does nothing
whenever the window does not contain today is a control that lies about what it
does. That argument is kept and narrowed rather than reversed: the button is
rendered exactly when today is inside the published window, which is the case
for every rolling link and for a fixed one that is currently running, and omitted
when there is nowhere for it to go. It is worth having back because a week and a
day view can be paged well away from today in a way a single month could not.
SharedCalendarRange::$today is the whole of the decision.

Variables:
  shared          SharedCalendarView   window, zone, and days keyed Y-m-d. Named
                                       `shared` because the shells call the
                                       CalendarView enum `view`
  range           SharedCalendarRange  this page: which view, its days, its
                                       placements and where its paging stops
  token           string               this link's own URL segment, for the links
  icsPath         string               where the same window is downloadable
  appearance      PublicAppearance     the owner's theme
  chipTimeFormat  string               a PHP date() format for a grid cell: compact
  rowTimeFormat   string               the same clock, spelled in full, for a row
  hourFormat      string               and again as an axis label, for the gutter
#}
{% extends 'sharing/_layout.html.twig' %}

{% block container_class %}max-w-3xl{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    {# Every link on this page names the same view and differs only in its date,
       or names the same date and differs only in its view. Built once here so
       the toolbar embed below stays a list of URLs rather than a nest of
       path() calls.

       `range.focus`, not `range.anchor`: the anchor is normalised to the view —
       the 1st for a month, Monday for a week — and a switcher built from it
       sent every month reader to day view of the 1st, which on a rolling
       window can be a day the link does not even publish. The focus is the
       date the reader actually asked about, clamped and nothing more. #}
    {% set viewUrls = {} %}
    {% for candidate in enum('App\\Domain\\Enum\\Calendar\\CalendarView').cases() %}
        {% set viewUrls = viewUrls|merge({
            (candidate.value): path('app_shared_calendar_show', {
                token: token,
                view: candidate.value,
                date: range.focus,
            }),
        }) %}
    {% endfor %}

    <header class="mb-4">
        <h1 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink">{{ 'calendar.share.heading'|trans }}</h1>

        {# `window_label`, not `window`. The latter is a two-child node —
           `window.fixed` and `window.rolling`, which the settings form uses for
           its radio labels — and asking the translator for the parent got the
           key itself printed on the page under the heading. It has said
           "calendar.share.window" to every recipient since the feature shipped;
           `bin/console debug:translation en --only-missing` lists it, which is
           where it was finally caught. #}
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-muted">
            {{ 'calendar.share.window_label'|trans({
                '%from%': shared.from|intl_date('dMMMy'),
                '%to%': shared.to|date_modify('-1 day')|intl_date('dMMMy'),
            }) }}
        </p>

        <div class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            {# Named on every page, not only when it differs from the reader's. The
               reader has no account here, so there is no stored preference to
               compare against, and a list of hours with no zone beside it is the
               single most reliable way to make somebody miss a meeting. #}
            <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg bg-sunken px-2.5 py-1 text-xs text-ink-muted">
                <i class="fa-regular fa-clock text-[10px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                {{ 'calendar.share.zone'|trans({ '%zone%': shared.zone }) }}
            </span>

            {% if shared.isBusyFreeOnly %}
                <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg bg-sunken px-2.5 py-1 text-xs text-ink-muted">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-eye-slash text-[10px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    {{ 'calendar.share.busy_free_only'|trans }}
                </span>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="rounded-pane border border-line overflow-hidden bg-surface">
        {# `spanLabel` for the agenda as well as the week: an agenda page here is
           a bounded slice of the published window rather than the authenticated
           agenda's endless rolling list, so its two ends are what "where you
           are" means. #}
        {% embed 'calendar/_toolbar_shell.html.twig' with {
            view:      range.view,
            anchor:    range.anchor,
            rangeFrom: range.from,
            rangeTo:   range.to,
            prevUrl:   range.previous is null ? null : path('app_shared_calendar_show', {
                           token: token, view: range.view.value, date: range.previous,
                       }),
            nextUrl:   range.next is null ? null : path('app_shared_calendar_show', {
                           token: token, view: range.view.value, date: range.next,
                       }),
            todayUrl:  range.today is null ? null : path('app_shared_calendar_show', {
                           token: token, view: range.view.value, date: range.today,
                       }),
            viewUrls:  viewUrls,
            spanLabel: range.view.value == 'week' or range.view.value == 'agenda',
        } %}{% endembed %}

        {% if range.view.value == 'month' %}
            {# `auto-rows` rather than the authenticated calendar's `h-full`: that
               grid lives in a pane with a height of its own to divide up, and this
               one is in a document that is as tall as it needs to be. A minimum per
               row is what stops a quiet month collapsing into six thin stripes. #}
            {% embed 'calendar/_month_shell.html.twig' with {
                dayKeys: range.dayKeys,
                days: range.gridDays,
                anchorMonth: range.anchor|date('n'),
                today: range.today ?? '',
                shellOuterClass: 'flex flex-col',
                shellRowsClass: 'auto-rows-[minmax(3.25rem,auto)] sm:auto-rows-[minmax(5.5rem,auto)]',
            } %}
                {% block cell_body %}
                    <div class="min-h-0 flex-1 space-y-0.5 overflow-hidden">
                        {% for entry in dayEntries|slice(0, 3) %}
                            {% include 'sharing/_entry_chip.html.twig' with {
                                entry: entry,
                                zone: shared.zone,
                                timeFormat: chipTimeFormat,
                            } only %}
                        {% endfor %}

                        {% if dayEntries|length > 3 %}
                            {# A count and not a link. The authenticated cell links
                               to its own day view here; this one would too, except
                               that a spill-in cell of a month grid can be a day the
                               window does not publish, and a "3 more" that led to a
                               dimmed empty day would be worse than a number. The
                               switcher above reaches the day view for any date the
                               link covers. #}
                            <p class="px-0.5 sm:px-1.5 text-[10px] sm:text-[11px] text-ink-faint">
                                {{ 'calendar.more_count'|trans({ '%count%': dayEntries|length - 3 }) }}
                            </p>
                        {% endif %}
                    </div>
                {% endblock %}
            {% endembed %}

        {% elseif range.view.isTimeGrid %}
            {# A height, because a document has none to divide up and 24 hours of
               rows would otherwise run the page to about 1200px of mostly empty
               grid with the legend and the subscribe link below the fold. The
               shell scrolls inside it and keeps its headings pinned, which is
               what it does inside the owner's pane. #}
            <div class="h-[32rem] sm:h-[36rem]">
                {% embed 'calendar/_time_grid_shell.html.twig' with {
                    dayKeys: range.dayKeys,
                    grid: range.grid,
                    zone: shared.zone,
                    today: range.today ?? '',
                    hourFormat: hourFormat,
                } %}
                    {% block all_day_entry %}
                        {% include 'sharing/_entry_chip.html.twig' with {
                            entry: entry,
                            zone: shared.zone,
                            timeFormat: chipTimeFormat,
                        } only %}
                    {% endblock %}

                    {# No attributes block filled: a block on this grid has no
                       event id, no recurrence id and nothing to drag, because a
                       SharedOccurrence has no path back to the row it came from.
                       That is the DTO's design, and it is why this page can
                       render the same grid the owner drags events around in. #}
                    {% block timed_entry %}
                        {% include 'sharing/_entry_chip.html.twig' with {
                            entry: entry,
                            zone: shared.zone,
                            timeFormat: chipTimeFormat,
                            tall: true,
                        } only %}
                    {% endblock %}

                    {% block column_unpublished %}
                        <span class="rounded bg-surface/80 px-1 py-0.5 text-[10px] leading-tight text-ink-faint text-center">
                            {{ 'calendar.share.not_shared'|trans }}
                        </span>
                    {% endblock %}
                {% endembed %}
            </div>

        {% else %}
            {# `showEmptyDays` is the property the page's old day list was built
               around, kept inside the view that replaced it. See _agenda_shell's
               header for why the owner's own agenda does the opposite. #}
            {% embed 'calendar/_agenda_shell.html.twig' with {
                dayKeys: range.dayKeys,
                days: range.gridDays,
                today: range.today ?? '',
                showEmptyDays: true,
            } %}
                {% block day_entries %}
                    <ul class="divide-y divide-line">
                        {% for entry in dayEntries %}
                            {% include 'sharing/_entry_row.html.twig' with {
                                entry: entry,
                                zone: shared.zone,
                                timeFormat: rowTimeFormat,
                            } only %}
                        {% endfor %}
                    </ul>
                {% endblock %}

                {% block day_empty %}
                    <p class="text-sm text-ink-faint italic">{{ 'calendar.share.day_free'|trans }}</p>
                {% endblock %}

                {# Only reachable when the page holds no published day at all,
                   which the clamping makes very hard to arrive at — kept because
                   a list with no rows must say something rather than be a blank
                   panel. #}
                {% block empty_state %}
                    <p class="px-4 py-10 text-center text-sm text-ink-faint italic">
                        {{ 'calendar.share.empty'|trans }}
                    </p>
                {% endblock %}
            {% endembed %}
        {% endif %}
    </section>

    <p class="mt-2 flex items-center gap-1.5 text-[11px] text-ink-faint">
        <span class="inline-block w-3 h-3 rounded-sm bg-sunken/20 border border-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        {{ 'calendar.share.outside_window'|trans }}
    </p>

    {# About the whole window rather than this page: a link with nothing in it
       anywhere should say so once, on whichever view the reader lands on, rather
       than leave them paging through a fortnight of empty days to find out. #}
    {% if shared.isEmpty %}
        <p class="mt-6 rounded-pane border border-line px-4 py-10 text-center text-sm text-ink-faint italic">
            {{ 'calendar.share.empty'|trans }}
        </p>
    {% endif %}

    <footer class="mt-8 flex items-center justify-between gap-3 text-xs text-ink-faint">
        <a href="{{ icsPath }}"
           class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-field bg-field px-2.5 py-1.5 font-medium text-ink-soft hover:bg-hover transition-colors">
            <i class="fa-regular fa-calendar-plus text-[10px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            {{ 'calendar.share.subscribe'|trans }}
        </a>

        <span>{{ 'calendar.share.footer'|trans }}</span>
    </footer>
{% endblock %}
